# Story bundles are tracked: they are the approval history and there is no
# second copy of them. Only the text is — the rendered halves below are large,
# binary, and regenerable from the text plus a paid call. Same reasoning as
# assets/sfx_cache/ further down, and the same deadline: cheap to decide now,
# impossible to undo after the first `record` commits an mp3.
stories/*/audio/
stories/*/images/
stories/*/video/
stories/*/*.srt

ambience/
sweep*.log
# Generated SFX, keyed by prompt hash and reused across every project. Ignored
# deliberately, not by oversight: it is unbounded binary that git cannot forget
# once committed, and every entry is regenerable from the prompt in concept.json.
# Regenerating costs money, so back the directory up outside git. Reverse this by
# deleting these two lines — cheap now, expensive after the first commit.
assets/sfx_cache/
!assets/sfx_cache/.gitkeep

# Timestamped backups left by `python3 -m ledger.migrate`. Keep them on disk
# until a migration is confirmed good; there is no reason to commit them.
ledger/*.bak.csv

# Job state from the review UI: one directory per run, holding the stage's log
# and its meta.json. Local to whichever machine ran the stage, and deliberately
# not under stories/ — mw-commit-stories commits that wholesale every fifteen
# minutes, and a job log is not approval history.
runs/

config.yaml
.env
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# Audition renders from `python3 -m ambience_pipeline.synth`. Regenerable from a
# seed in one command, and large.
auditions/

calibration-sweep.sh
cleanup.sh
config.yaml.bak
oauth.txt
working/


	